>> title: Lamb Tagine
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: lamb, moroccan, apricots, oven, braise
>> counters: Shawarma Counter, One Pot
>> aka: lamb tajine, tajine, Moroccan lamb stew
>> pairs-with: harissa
>> servings: 6
>> time: 3 hr 30 min
>> slack: forgiving — the apricots go in for the last half hour; from the start they dissolve into the sauce and are gone

Preheat the #oven{} to 325°F (160°C).

Toss @lamb shoulder{3%lb}(1.4 kg; cut in 2-in pieces), @ground cumin{2%tsp}, @ground coriander{2%tsp}, @ground cinnamon{1%tsp}, @ground ginger{1%tsp}, @kosher salt{2%tsp} in a #bowl{}.

Brown @&(~1)spiced lamb{}, @olive oil{3%Tbs} in a #tagine{}.

Soften @yellow onions{2%large}(sliced), @garlic{4%cloves} with @&(~1)browned lamb{}.

>> step: braise 325°F 2 hr
Braise @&(~1)tagine{} with @chicken stock{2%cup}(475 mL) at 325°F for ~{2%hr}.

>> step: add apricots, braise 30 min more
Add @dried apricots{1%cup}(150 g), @honey{2%Tbs} to @&(~1)braised lamb{} and braise ~{30%min}.
